stream
BT
/F1 18 Tf
50 760 Td
(Kafka Interview Guide) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 735 Td
(1. Kafka basics) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 720 Td
(Producer: sends records to topics, chooses target partition, batches data, and uses acks for reliability.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 708 Td
(Consumer: reads from partitions with offsets, works in consumer groups, and each partition is processed by one consumer in a group.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 696 Td
(Topic: logical stream of events. Partition: ordered log segment with offsets and parallelism. Broker: Kafka server process.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 684 Td
(Storage: data is persisted to disk and replicated across brokers for durability and recovery.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 660 Td
(2. Zookeeper working) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 645 Td
(Zookeeper maintains broker metadata, election state, membership, and leadership coordination in older Kafka deployments.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 633 Td
(Leader election: controller watches broker liveness and picks a new leader from the ISR when a leader fails.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 621 Td
(Follower election: followers replicate leader log and become eligible when they are caught up and in sync.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 597 Td
(3. KRaft working) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 582 Td
(KRaft removes ZooKeeper and uses Raft-based consensus for metadata quorum and leadership election.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 570 Td
(Leader election: a quorum elects a leader using term numbers and heartbeats. Followers replicate metadata logs.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 558 Td
(Modern Kafka uses KRaft for simpler operations and no external coordination service.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 534 Td
(4. Kafka brokers) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 519 Td
(Brokers receive producer writes, serve consumer reads, store partitions, replicate data, and maintain cluster state.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 507 Td
(Important broker configs: listeners, advertised.listeners, log.dirs, num.io.threads, log.retention.hours, and replica.fetch.max.bytes.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 483 Td
(5. Interview Q&A) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 468 Td
(Q: What is Kafka? A: Distributed streaming platform for real-time event delivery, durability, and scalable data pipelines.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 456 Td
(Q: What is consumer group? A: Set of consumers that together read a topic, each partition handled by one consumer in the group.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 444 Td
(Q: What is ISR? A: In-Sync Replicas, replicas caught up sufficiently to become a leader.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 432 Td
(Q: Why use Kafka? A: High throughput, decoupling, replayability, fault tolerance, and horizontal scaling.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 420 Td
(Q: What is offset? A: Unique position of a record in a partition.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 396 Td
(6. Scenario-based questions) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 381 Td
(Scenario: consumer lag is rising. Answer: scale consumers, add partitions, fix processing bottlenecks, and monitor lag.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 369 Td
(Scenario: broker down. Answer: followers continue serving reads if replication is healthy and leadership fails over.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 357 Td
(Scenario: data loss. Answer: verify acks=all, replication factor, min.insync.replicas, and retries.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 345 Td
(Scenario: duplicate reads. Answer: Kafka is at-least-once by default, so consumers need deduplication logic.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 321 Td
(7. Do's and Dont's) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 306 Td
(Do: use replication factor 3, monitor lag, keep partitions aligned to consumer parallelism, and use acks=all for critical topics.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 294 Td
(Dont: ignore under-replicated partitions, run single-broker production, or misconfigure topic partitions.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 270 Td
(8. Producer, consumer, topic configs) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 255 Td
(Producer: bootstrap.servers, acks, retries, linger.ms, batch.size, compression.type, enable.idempotence.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 243 Td
(Consumer: group.id, auto.offset.reset, enable.auto.commit, max.poll.records, session.timeout.ms, isolation.level.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 231 Td
(Topic: num.partitions, replication.factor, retention.ms, cleanup.policy, min.insync.replicas.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 11 Tf
50 207 Td
(9. Monitoring and Prometheus) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 192 Td
(Monitor: consumer lag, broker CPU, disk usage, replication lag, under-replicated partitions, bytes in and out, and request latency.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 180 Td
(Prometheus scrape config: static_configs targets: [broker1:7071, broker2:7071, broker3:7071].) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 168 Td
(JMX exporter exposes Kafka metrics, which Grafana visualizes for performance and scalability.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 156 Td
(Production tip: keep quorum, broker health, lag, and storage usage under constant watch.) Tj
ET
BT
/F1 9.5 Tf
50 144 Td
(This PDF is a compact summary of the Kafka guide created for interview preparation and production understanding.) Tj
ET
